Relevant columns and potential usage
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."System": filter to NPM packages.  
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."Name": exclude rows where name contains “@”.  
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."Version": pick the concrete release we are examining.  
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."VersionInfo": JSON – field "IsRelease" (true ⇒ real release) and "Ordinal" (can be used to find the newest release).  
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."Links": JSON array – flatten to pull objects whose "Label" = 'SOURCE_REPO' and whose "URL" contains 'github.com'.  
• DEPENDENCIES."System", "Name", "Version", "Dependency": count how many dependency rows belong to a package version.  
• DEPENDENCIES."SnapshotAt" / PACKAGEVERSIONS."SnapshotAt": use a common snapshot or simply work inside the same version values.  

Main conditions we will need
1. PACKAGEVERSIONS."System" = 'NPM'  
2. PACKAGEVERSIONS."Name" NOT ILIKE '%@%'  
3. PACKAGEVERSIONS."VersionInfo":"IsRelease"::BOOLEAN = TRUE  
4. DEPENDENCIES."System" = 'NPM' (to match)  
5. LINK flatten filter: f.value:"Label"::STRING = 'SOURCE_REPO' and f.value:"URL"::STRING ILIKE '%github.com%'  

Below are ten exploratory ⇒ increasingly‑complex Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) to travel from simple inspection to the final answer pattern.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few NPM package‑version rows and their raw JSON columns.
SELECT
  "SnapshotAt",
  "Name",
  "Version",
  "VersionInfo",
  "Links"
FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS
WHERE "System" = 'NPM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect how the "Links" array looks when flattened.
SELECT
  p."Name",
  p."Version",
  f.value:"Label"::STRING  AS "Label",
  f.value:"URL"::STRING    AS "URL"
FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."Links") f
WHERE p."System" = 'NPM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Only SOURCE_REPO GitHub links, still sample view.
SELECT
  p."Name",
  p."Version",
  f.value:"URL"::STRING AS "GitHubURL"
FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."Links") f
WHERE p."System" = 'NPM'
  AND f.value:"Label"::STRING = 'SOURCE_REPO'
  AND f.value:"URL"::STRING ILIKE '%github.com%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Look at dependency rows for NPM packages (raw view).
SELECT
  "Name",
  "Version",
  "Dependency"
FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPENDENCIES
WHERE "System" = 'NPM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Count how many dependency rows exist per (name,version) pair.
SELECT
  "Name",
  "Version",
  COUNT(*) AS "DepsCount"
FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPENDENCIES
WHERE "System" = 'NPM'
GROUP BY "Name","Version"
ORDER BY "DepsCount" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Restrict to releases (IsRelease = true) and names without '@'.
SELECT
  p."Name",
  p."Version",
  p."VersionInfo":"IsRelease"::BOOLEAN AS "IsRelease"
FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS p
WHERE p."System" = 'NPM'
  AND p."Name" NOT ILIKE '%@%'
  AND p."VersionInfo":"IsRelease"::BOOLEAN = TRUE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Pick the latest release (highest ordinal) for each package.
WITH rel AS (
  SELECT
    "Name",
    "Version",
    "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER AS "Ord",
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "Name"
                       ORDER BY "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER DESC NULLS LAST) AS rn
  FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS
  WHERE "System" = 'NPM'
    AND "Name" NOT ILIKE '%@%'
    AND "VersionInfo":"IsRelease"::BOOLEAN = TRUE
)
SELECT "Name","Version","Ord"
FROM rel
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Combine previous CTE with dependency counts for those "latest releases".
WITH latest AS (
  SELECT
    "Name",
    "Version"
  FROM (
    SELECT
      "Name",
      "Version",
      "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER AS ord,
      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "Name"
                         ORDER BY "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER DESC NULLS LAST) AS rn
    FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS
    WHERE "System" = 'NPM'
      AND "Name" NOT ILIKE '%@%'
      AND "VersionInfo":"IsRelease"::BOOLEAN = TRUE
  )
  WHERE rn = 1
)
SELECT
  d."Name",
  d."Version",
  COUNT(*) AS "DepsCount"
FROM latest l
JOIN DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPENDENCIES d
  ON d."System"  = 'NPM'
 AND d."Name"    = l."Name"
 AND d."Version" = l."Version"
GROUP BY d."Name", d."Version"
ORDER BY "DepsCount" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Pull GitHub SOURCE_REPO links for the top‑N package‑versions
--    (those with the largest dependency counts from step 8).
WITH latest AS (
  SELECT
    "Name",
    "Version"
  FROM (
    SELECT
      "Name",
      "Version",
      "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER AS ord,
      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "Name"
                         ORDER BY "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER DESC NULLS LAST) AS rn
    FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS
    WHERE "System" = 'NPM'
      AND "Name" NOT ILIKE '%@%'
      AND "VersionInfo":"IsRelease"::BOOLEAN = TRUE
  )
  WHERE rn = 1
),
deps AS (
  SELECT
    d."Name",
    d."Version",
    COUNT(*) AS deps_cnt
  FROM latest l
  JOIN DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPENDENCIES d
    ON d."System"  = 'NPM'
   AND d."Name"    = l."Name"
   AND d."Version" = l."Version"
  GROUP BY d."Name", d."Version"
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT
    "Name",
    "Version",
    deps_cnt,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY deps_cnt DESC) AS rn
  FROM deps
)
SELECT
  r."Name",
  r."Version",
  r.deps_cnt,
  f.value:"URL"::STRING AS "GitHubURL"
FROM ranked r
JOIN DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS p
  ON p."System"  = 'NPM'
 AND p."Name"    = r."Name"
 AND p."Version" = r."Version",
 LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."Links") f
WHERE r.rn <= 10
  AND f.value:"Label"::STRING = 'SOURCE_REPO'
  AND f.value:"URL"::STRING ILIKE '%github.com%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final single‑row query – GitHub URL for the package whose
--     latest released version has the highest dependency count (name has no '@').
WITH latest AS (
  SELECT
    "Name",
    "Version"
  FROM (
    SELECT
      "Name",
      "Version",
      "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER AS ord,
      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "Name"
                         ORDER BY "VersionInfo":"Ordinal"::INTEGER DESC NULLS LAST) AS rn
    FROM DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS
    WHERE "System" = 'NPM'
      AND "Name" NOT ILIKE '%@%'
      AND "VersionInfo":"IsRelease"::BOOLEAN = TRUE
  )
  WHERE rn = 1
),
deps AS (
  SELECT
    d."Name",
    d."Version",
    COUNT(*) AS deps_cnt
  FROM latest l
  JOIN DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPENDENCIES d
    ON d."System"  = 'NPM'
   AND d."Name"    = l."Name"
   AND d."Version" = l."Version"
  GROUP BY d."Name", d."Version"
),
max_pkg AS (
  SELECT
    "Name",
    "Version",
    deps_cnt
  FROM deps
  QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY deps_cnt DESC) = 1
)
SELECT
  m."Name",
  m."Version",
  m.deps_cnt,
  f.value:"URL"::STRING AS "GitHubURL"
FROM max_pkg m
JOIN DEPS_DEV_V1.DEPS_DEV_V1.PACKAGEVERSIONS p
  ON p."System"  = 'NPM'
 AND p."Name"    = m."Name"
 AND p."Version" = m."Version",
 LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."Links") f
WHERE f.value:"Label"::STRING = 'SOURCE_REPO'
  AND f.value:"URL"::STRING ILIKE '%github.com%'
LIMIT 20;
```

Each successive query builds understanding and culminates in the final statement that returns the desired GitHub SOURCE_REPO link for the qualifying NPM package with the most dependencies in its newest released version.
